now to the alarming spread of the  coronavirus over the holidays for the  past week the united states is averaging  more than 277  000 new covet cases a day it's a  battering end to 2021 forcing many  people to reconsider their new year's  eve plans nikki batis is with us nikki  what are you hearing good morning vlad  good morning well two years into the  pandemic new york state smashed its  daily covet cases record with more than  67 thousand new positive tests in just  24 hours that's a 65 percent increase in  one day the sky-high number of cases  across the country has experts urging  people to change their plans for new  year's eve  as cities prep for new year's eve  celebrations dr falchi joined other  experts wednesday urging people to skip  out on large gatherings this year what i  would suggest people do not do  is to go to very large 50 to 60 person  parties where people are blowing  whistles and all that sort of thing  and celebrating and you don't know  the vaccination status of the people in  that environment in the last week  hospitalizations increased 14 percent  with a seven-day average of 9 000 per  day with pediatric hospitalizations  being some of the most significant  increases up nearly 50 percent in  several states the surge in coronavirus  cases has pushed city leaders nationwide  to significantly scale back or cancel  new year's eve plans altogether  atlanta's 32-year tradition the peach  drop has been canceled again  san francisco also scrap plans for their  fireworks show  and while the iconic times square ball  drop will still host thousands of party  goers it will look drastically different  than past years all participants must be  fully vaccinated and masked and they  have limited capacity to allow for more  social distancing  are you vaccinated are you boosted and  have you been wearing your mask cdc  director dr rochelle wolinski advised  that even for those gathering in smaller  settings precautions are essential  ideally if people are coming together  you'd have everybody take a test before  they gather if they were intending to  take off their masks and if you have a  large gathering i wouldn't even take off  your mask in that situation despite  guidance testing is still not readily  available to everyone who wants it  leaving people facing long lines and  empty shelves  despite the record-setting number of  coveted cases dr wolinski continues to  defend the cdc's decision to cut  isolation time from 10 days to 5 days  for those infected with covid without  needing a negative test saying in part  these isolation timelines were more  realistic for people to follow  nikki thank you now
 

